# Installed by the reac-pw RPM as /usr/lib/systemd/user-preset/90-reac-pw.preset.
#
# NOT AUTO-APPLIED BY THE PACKAGE, SINCE 1.0.19. `%post` used to run this preset with
# `systemctl --no-reload preset --global`, which is not scoped to the user running the
# install: it enables the unit for EVERY systemd --user instance on the host, present
# or future -- including one `sudo` spawns for root the moment it next runs. Measured
# 2026-09-18: exactly that started a second reac-pw under root, which won the segment
# lock the console user's own daemon needed. `%post` no longer calls this file at all
# (packaging/reac-pw.spec).
#
# It stays packaged for an operator who wants `systemctl --user preset-all` (no
# --global: scoped to their OWN session only) instead of a plain `enable --now`; both
# land on the same unit. Numbered ahead of the distro's catch-all
# 99-default-disable.preset (systemd presets are first-file-wins per unit), so this
# line decides reac-pw.service and the disable-everything default never reaches it.
#
# This does not fight the packaged reac-pw-master.service: that unit and this one
# `Conflicts=` each other in the unit file itself (packaging/reac-pw.service), and
# openmixer's arbitration spec retired reac-pw-master.service on 2026-09-02 --
# nothing installs it any more. See README.md and docs/design/specs (openmixer repo)
# 2026-08-20-reac-master-arbitration.md, amendment 2026-09-02 (second), rule f.
enable reac-pw.service
